{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e","id":1418620,"title":"[Fanon Thread] How to update the Sabbat to 5E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-16T18:12:22-07:00","id":1418620,"title":"[Fanon Thread] How to update the Sabbat to 5E","content":"Pretty much what the title says.<br /> <br /> You have been given the job of finally doing a Sabbat book (or participating in it) for 5th Edition by Modiphius. Your job is to bring the Sabbat back into prominence as a major faction for the setting as established.<br /> <br /> Things that have been previously established have to remain canon. There was a Gehenna War, quite a lot of Lasombra defected to the Camarilla, the Harbingers have taken over the Clan formerly known as the Giovanni, and at least some of its major cities have fallen (Mexico City and Montreal). Everything else is up to you and you can interpret what you want from it as well. For instance, if you want, have the city of Montreal taken back. You have complete freedom to suggest the changes you want and what you think would be pretty awesome to do.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be fluff alone either. Your suggestion can be reimplement the Path system or adapt them as optional rules. Also, that Sabbat, due to the ritae are immune to the automatic Humanity loss of diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T18:22:15-07:00","id":1418622,"title":"","content":"<b>Rules Update Suggestions</b><br /> <br /> 1. Sabbat automatically get the option to have <b>Vampire Convictions</b> as one of their base abilities. Vampire Convictions work identically to Convictions in the Camarilla and Anarchs but can have Touchstones that are their fellow vampires. In fact, they are forbidden from having Human Touchstones.<br /> <br /> 2. Sabbat have <b>Path</b> rather than <b>Humanity</b> on their character sheet.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Vampire Touchstones</b> are usually their Pack mates but can also be vampires who they revere as exemplars of the kind of undead they want to be.<br /> <br /> 4. Sabbat do not lose a point of Path if they diablerize a Camarilla, Ashira, Inconnu, or Anarch. This is just part of the perks of the sect.<br /> <br /> 5. Sabbat do not lose a point of Path if they kill a human or engage in mayhem. This is just part of the Chronicle tenets of any Sabbat game.<br /> <br /> 6. Sabbat do get stains for betraying the Sect, betraying their fellow Pack members, blasphemy against the sect, showing mercy, showing weakness, or displaying cowardice. Basically, your religion should be like an undead Klingon.<br /> <br /> 7. I am trying to think up a good adjustment for bestial frenzies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T19:19:53-07:00","id":1418623,"title":"","content":"For the record, I would prefer to see an Ashirra book come out first. <br /> <br /> First 100-130 pages or so fiction and setting. Topics to cover, 2nd Inquisition attacks on Sabbat strongholds, stories from packs that went to the war and packs that didn't, how life in the Sabbat is different after returning from the war and attempting to rebuild. Rites and rituals described in the fiction. Some light mechanics<br /> <br /> Next 50ish pages clans of the Sabbat, give more weight to Shimmies, remaining Lasombra and how the rest of the clan leaving has changed their place in the hierarchy, and Panders highlighting what truly makes them different than Caitiff in other Sects. Selective Antitribu section covering House Goatrix, City Gangrel, and how being demoted to third-tier (fourth tier?) has changed the sects viewpoints on their place in vampire society.<br /> <br /> A couple of pages on pack/sect conflict resolution.<br /> <br /> Loresheets, including taking Paths of Englightent as a Loresheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T20:16:29-07:00","id":1418631,"title":"","content":"I would have them trim down the Auctoritas Ritae to Creation Rites, Fire Dance, Monomacy, Vaulderie, War Party, Wild Hunt. They would elevate the Ignoblis Ritae One of My Tribe to an Auctoritas Ritae. Seven total. Participation in Ritae, as well as Vinculums, may take the place of Touchstones (I like the idea of a vampire doing something that might grant Stains and going, 'this is bad, but I walked through fire last week so I can manage'). I also like the idea of Packmates acting as Touchstones too.<br /> <br /> The core unit of the Sabbat would be the Pack. Embracing with the blood of the Pack would become a thing again. Thanks to their experience in the Gehenna War, returning Sabbat will not be so gung ho about Diablerie. The War Party Auctoritas would provide a means of mitigating Humanity loss due to Diablerie. <br /> <br /> There will be internal conflict with returning Sabbat and those that stayed. As veterans come home from war, they no longer fit in with their 'civilian' counterparts and indeed, see much of what they do night to night as pointless after what they've been through. Similar to the returning mortals who join motorcycle clubs, the only place these Sabbat feel at home is with their Pack.<br /> <br /> The Black Hand will be making inroads to trim the fat and turn the remaining Sabbat into its own vision of what it should be. Part of why the Sabbat began abandoning cities was not just to go fight the Gehenna War. The Black Hand started to refuse answering calls, leaving cities to stand or fall on their own. This also ties in with the Lasombra defection.<br /> <br /> I'd use Ethics and some of the Hierarchy of Sins as examples of Convictions for Path followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T22:16:07-07:00","id":1418637,"title":"","content":"The Paths of Enlightenment homebrew is an excellent start: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z...ymRB7vteu/view</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T23:33:51-07:00","id":1418640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I would prefer to see an Ashirra book come out first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I surely agree, we need some sort of clarification on the Ashirra since the Beckoning is all centered in the Middle-East at the moment and apparently the MAJORITY of the Sabbat have gone over there (along with the majority of all the Elders from all the sects apparently too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T23:51:06-07:00","id":1418641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418640#post1418640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I surely agree, we need some sort of clarification on the Ashirra since the Beckoning is all centered in the Middle-East at the moment and apparently the MAJORITY of the Sabbat have gone over there (along with the majority of all the Elders from all the sects apparently too).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this weird image of the Ashirra and its vampires sitting in their perfectly normal cities, drinking tea, and watching television while 30 miles outside there's this apocalyptic Mad Max-esque war going on.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that's weird.&quot; - Deborah, 13th generation Israeli Banu Haqim Vizier.<br /> <br /> Mind you, having an experience with evangelical missionaries and pilgrims, I know that at least some are going to disbelieve the Beckoning exists and claim it's just a Kindred version of Jerusalem syndrome.<br /> <br /> &quot;Right, the Elders of the Camarilla are all summoned by an invisible force.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, it's true! It's GEHENNA!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure it is, pal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T00:01:49-07:00","id":1418643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418641#post1418641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have this weird image of the Ashirra and its vampires sitting in their perfectly normal cities, drinking tea, and watching television while 30 miles outside there's this apocalyptic Mad Max-esque war going on.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Well, that's weird.&amp;quot; - Deborah, 13th generation Israeli Banu Haqim Vizier.<br /> <br /> Mind you, having an experience with evangelical missionaries and pilgrims, I know that at least some are going to disbelieve the Beckoning exists and claim it's just a Kindred version of Jerusalem syndrome.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Right, the Elders of the Camarilla are all summoned by an invisible force.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;No, it's true! It's GEHENNA!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Sure it is, pal.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> They all watch Outer Banks and chill while Rome burns...<br /> <br /> What\u2019s Jerusalem Syndrome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T00:27:13-07:00","id":1418645,"title":"","content":"So... <br /> <br /> The Camarilla elders had this idea that the masses of neonates were too much and they wanted to call an exterminatus on most of them. The Sabbat elders agreed. Also this new-world the Camarilla had in mind appealed to the Sabbat elders and so...<br /> A bunch of elders get 'beckoned' and by that I mean they don't really agree with the idea and go into hiding because they don't want to be persecuted by either side<br /> The Brujah left the Camarilla because they didn't like the idea. Which is ridiculous, because no-one brujah is going to decide something that big for all of them, but I've gotta work with what's written. <br /> The Camarilla kicked out a bunch of it's members.<br /> The Camarilla allowed open religion to appeal to the Sabbat elders and get them more on board with the whole thing<br /> The Sabbat are sending their members on a crusade<br /> The Camarilla organized some hunters to begin a cull.<br /> The Sabbat are killing their members in the shipping crates. <br /> The Tremere split to get into every city: Carna for the new camarilla cities who hate them, Ipps for the Anarch domains, Gor to keep an eye on the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat members who survived shipping will go on a grand crusade of vengance, some of the loyal moles they left behind will be very useful. <br /> <br /> Of course, this sounds all too clever. Maybe I'd just have the Sabbat come back as antediluvian puppets and have them abduct everyone as sacrifices to their antediluvian overlords before they too get chomped. <br /> Or maybe, because i've got a sense of humour, I'll have the Sabbat win. They kill all the Antes and ponder upon what to do. Then people eat the guys who ate the old third gens, then people eat those guys, then people eat those guys, and so on. Then the Sabbat is about a dozen people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T00:41:13-07:00","id":1418646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418643#post1418643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> They all watch Outer Banks and chill while Rome burns...</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit to a certain level of humor at the fact that the Gehenna War seems to depend on the Middle East being a mysterious and far off land as opposed to a place I can check on my Google satellite feed and chat with people from every day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What\u2019s Jerusalem Syndrome? </div> </div> </div>Jerusalem Syndrome is a thing that's pretty well known among missionaries and tourists to Israel. Basically, and I'm obviously simplifying it, they go batshit from exposure to the Holy Land and decide that they're playing out some role in Biblical prophecy. John Q. Public decides he's Jesus, Moses Reborn, or having a personal mission from God to give up all his possessions and preach on the streets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerusalem_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/17/Jerusalem_Syndrome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerusalem_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\"> Jerusalem syndrome - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerusalem_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerusalem_syndrome </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the vampire context, it would be that the Ashirra think 1999 and 2004 really screwed with a bunch of Elder's heads and they're all heading to fight in Gehenna based on their own devotion to prophecy.<br /> <br /> Which is a hilarious and not ENTIRELY inconceivable idea actually:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;The Thin Bloods have appeared. The millennium has changed. The stars are right and the planet is dying. Gehenna is upon us!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Uh, Menele, are you feeling alright?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No! I must go to Carthage and raise my sire! It is time to fight the war!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I think you should reconsider--&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>*Presence 9*</b> All the childer and childer's childer I am a few generations close to along with all of my old allies, JOIN ME IN CARTHAGE TO FIGHT THE WAR!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> *over in London*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Restored Mithras: Menele has gone to the Middle East with an army of Methuselahs and Elders! IT MUST BE GEHENNA! SUMMON MY ARMIES <b>*Dominate 9* </b>Join me in Syria!</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T02:48:00-07:00","id":1418647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418641#post1418641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have this weird image of the Ashirra and its vampires sitting in their perfectly normal cities, drinking tea, and watching television while 30 miles outside there's this apocalyptic Mad Max-esque war going on.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that's weird.&quot; - Deborah, 13th generation Israeli Banu Haqim Vizier.<br /> <br /> Mind you, having an experience with evangelical missionaries and pilgrims, I know that at least some are going to disbelieve the Beckoning exists and claim it's just a Kindred version of Jerusalem syndrome.<br /> <br /> &quot;Right, the Elders of the Camarilla are all summoned by an invisible force.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, it's true! It's GEHENNA!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure it is, pal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> looooooooool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T04:36:07-07:00","id":1418650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e#post1418620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what the title says.<br /> <br /> You have been given the job of finally doing a Sabbat book (or participating in it) for 5th Edition by Modiphius. Your job is to bring the Sabbat back into prominence as a major faction for the setting as established.<br /> <br /> Things that have been previously established have to remain canon. There was a Gehenna War, quite a lot of Lasombra defected to the Camarilla, the Harbingers have taken over the Clan formerly known as the Giovanni, and at least some of its major cities have fallen (Mexico City and Montreal).</div> </div> </div> </div><b>lore-wise</b>, I guess considering the speed at which all the events happened, the remaining sabbat would be a mix of confused and unnerved,<br /> I wouldn't bring them back to prominence, just have them stuck in this loop of tryig to figure out what happened and trying to figure out what to do,<br /> <br /> they'd be mostly improvising, hanging out on anarch territory or squatting among the camarilla,<br /> the SI activity has cut or slowed down their communications with the rest of the sect,<br /> having lost Mexico and Montreal, they have lost most of their war ressources and blood magic assistance,<br /> <br /> but on the bright side, the semi-collapse of the Tremere has affoarded them some room to maneuver<br /> <br /> in America, Serpents of the Light would probably have some connections or downright join the Ministry,<br /> the Black Angels communities in America would be strugling due to lasombra defectors hunting them down, and the rise of some strange lasombra cults in the camarilla,<br /> the seven fires efforts are mostly unsuccessful, as they only manage to eleminate and catch entry level vampires and other weaklings holding weak intel with limited reach,<br /> <br /> in Europe and North Africa, the Black Hand and some sabbat elders, having their hands full with the crusades, decide to hire some sabbat to re-establish connection with the rest of the sect,<br /> most of these sabbat either have no stake in the war or lost everything in the recent events and would be willing to do mercenary work for the right price,<br /> they're a bit disorganized at first and struggling with the new environment but eventually make it to America,<br /> they make contact with the Black Angels, the sabbat in anarch territory and learn about sabbat militants called the Seven,<br /> <br /> upon first contact, the Seven are mistrusting of the mercenaries, especially when they find out no support is coming from the east,<br /> but after some joint operations and sharing some good old ritae, the Seven finally accept to give what little intel they gathered and safe routes they established to allow the mercs to look for other cells in Canada and Latin America<br /> <br /> if successful, the black hand and eastern sabbat try to coordinate the sabbat in the west, and send some (meager) support to America<br /> <br /> <b>mechanics-wise</b>...I don't know, I've been trying to think up some new rules, but I'm bad at making those,<br /> <br /> mostly, I'm interrested in making some path mechanics separate from the humanity system to give the sabbat some flavour,<br /> my first attempt would be to think up how the gnostic sabbat (Cathari) would differ from the Church of Caine and the Ministry,<br /> I was thinking some mechanics that would emphasize the Cathari being &quot;material beings&quot; locking and leeching from the spritiual","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-17-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T04:48:10-07:00","id":1418651,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> yeah, that is kinda funny lol. But for real, I always figured the Gehenna War was fought in the shadows, out of sight of not just the mortals but the Ashirra who actually lived there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T08:10:29-07:00","id":1418662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418623#post1418623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I would prefer to see an Ashirra book come out first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. And an Ashirra would also provide info on the Sabbat, as a lot of Sabbat are (or were) running around in the local deserts like a bunch of jackasses.<br /> <br /> It is also interesting to think that the Beckoning mostly hits non-Ashirra vampires.<br /> <br /> As for the Sabbat;<ul><li>The \u201cold\u201d Sabbat is gone.</li> <li>There are a half dozen or so Sabbat survivor cells, each believing it to be carrying on the best and trustiest traditions and goals of the old Sabbat.</li> <li>Lucita is leading one such cell, probably the least objectionable (or at least most approachable and negotiable).</li> <li>The other cells range from worse to much worse, with some seeming to be little more than violent and cruel Anarchs to some cells actively trying to bring about the end of the world.</li> <li>One cell is composed entirely, or mostly, of Tzimisce and their servants.</li> <li>Vykos is missing but supposedly the head of a cult \u2013 but this might be a deception on part of others.</li> <li>CTPhipps mechanical suggestions are good.</li> <li>But in the general flexible (for the ST to use) and mystery, the Sabbat fulfills the same narrative role it had back in 1<sup>st</sup> edition and in part of 2<sup>nd</sup> edition; some generally unknowable enemy force, lurking in the darkness at the edges of the known\u2026 waiting to destroy the unwary.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T08:26:19-07:00","id":1418663,"title":"","content":"Some Loresheet Ideas:<br /> <br /> * <b>Black Hand</b>: Membership in this group would obviously be a important potential Loresheet.<br /> <br /> * <b>Diablerie</b>: Give the Sabbat a special relationship with diablerie that they can derive more benefit from it and perhaps even increase their Path rating through the ritualistic practice of the art.<br /> <br /> * <b>Famous Sabbat</b>: Polonia, Lucita, Vykos, and so on are all choices obviously.<br /> <br /> * <b>Games of Instinct</b>: You're famous and well-practiced at all these insane stunts that Sabbat do for prestige as well as to prove their courage.<br /> <br /> * <b>Gehenna Warrior</b>: You have been to the Middle East and SEEN things. You have emerged with a lot of experience in fighting Elders, Ancients, and carrying out military tactics against vampires.<br /> <br /> * <b>House Goratrix (Tremere Only)</b>: You are a member of House Goratrix and secretly working for Tremere.<br /> <br /> * <b>Pack Priest</b>: You have the ability to &quot;heal&quot; stains on your coterie's Path and do other rituals to keep them from wightdom or perhaps direct frenzy to useful ends.<br /> <br /> * <b>Sabbat Inquisition</b>: Pretty much the same as membership in the Black Hand. You are part of the Sabbat Inquisition and hunt infernalists.<br /> <br /> * <b>Secret Infernalist</b>: Because it's not the 80s anymore, you can play a character who is enslaved to or enslaves a demon. You have some infernal investments and can summon demons to benefit yourself, Blood Sorcery or no.<br /> <br /> * <b>Vinculum</b> which would have benefits like the ability to do the ritual, powerful bonds, the ability to establish said bonds but ignore them yourselves, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T09:10:29-07:00","id":1418669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418650#post1418650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> in America, Serpents of the Light would probably have some connections or downright join the Ministry,l</div> </div> </div> </div>So, like, what do the serpents of the light actually believe in besides a rainbow serpent? Lightness and goodness? I recall reading they had a sunlight spell...<br /> <br /> Because they were heretical to the OG followers of Set that were far, far, far closer to &quot;the ministry&quot; than &quot;the church of set&quot;. So i think it pretty unlikely that they would join the ministry who should still be their enemies, but then again I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T09:13:02-07:00","id":1418670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418669#post1418669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, like, what do the serpents of the light actually believe in besides a rainbow serpent? Lightness and goodness? I recall reading they had a sunlight spell...<br /> <br /> Because they were heretical to the OG followers of Set that were far, far, far closer to &quot;the ministry&quot; than &quot;the church of set&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really that complicated.<br /> <br /> * The Serpents of Light believe in Voodoo and Damballa as well as, you know, a non-evil religion. They're a Caribbean offshoot of the Followers that kept their original religion and joined the Sabbat to rebel against the Setites.<br /> <br /> * The Followers of Set believe in Set vs. all other gods (the evil Aeons).<br /> <br /> * The Ministry believes in a wide variety of religious and ecstatic practices while largely being polytheistic.<br /> <br /> Given the Ministry is polytheistic and doesn't necessarily believe in Set per se (or at least SET ALONE), the Church of Set finds this heresy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T11:16:09-07:00","id":1418680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418670#post1418670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * The Followers of Set believe in Set vs. all other gods (the evil Aeons).<br /> <br /> * The Ministry believes in a wide variety of religious and ecstatic practices while largely being polytheistic.<br /> <br /> Given the Ministry is polytheistic and doesn't necessarily believe in Set per se (or at least SET ALONE),.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hol' up. <br /> <br /> The ministry are now just a loose collection of religious groups that... do they still believe in corruption? <br /> <br /> What? <br /> <br /> So, essentially, there was a great, wonderful and glorious sect, the Followers of Set, with their own glorious religion of worshiping the many masks of Set and his roll as champion of the lineage and gnostic teacher. <br /> <br /> And they split it into two groups<br /> One who worships set for it's own sake and mostly wants to forget about why.<br /> and one which worships... what? Corruption? and by Polytheism, you mean like, Set and his children/consorts/close allies or you mean 'let's just have whatever pantheon we like' because it sounds like the latter. <br /> <br /> I feel like before we had a pancake and now we have a choice between raw eggs and flour. and yeah you could say religions have a tendancy to go to shit, but it hasn't been twenty years and vampires live for hundreds so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T11:56:11-07:00","id":1418682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418680#post1418680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hol' up.<br /> <br /> The ministry are now just a loose collection of religious groups that... do they still believe in corruption?<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> So, essentially, there was a great, wonderful and glorious sect, the Followers of Set, with their own glorious religion of worshiping the many masks of Set and his roll as champion of the lineage and gnostic teacher.<br /> <br /> And they split it into two groups<br /> One who worships set for it's own sake and mostly wants to forget about why.<br /> and one which worships... what? Corruption? and by Polytheism, you mean like, Set and his children/consorts/close allies or you mean 'let's just have whatever pantheon we like' because it sounds like the latter.<br /> <br /> I feel like before we had a pancake and now we have a choice between raw eggs and flour. and yeah you could say religions have a tendancy to go to shit, but it hasn't been twenty years and vampires live for hundreds so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's called <b>Reality Ensues</b> to quote TVtropes.org.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, you want us to abandon our 3000 year old worship of Kali, THAT PREDATES SET and our culture to say she's a fragment of your god. One who wasn't EVIL IN THE FIRST PLACE in Egyptian mythology and venerate corruption? That's stupid. Your religion is stupid. Oh and you're stupid.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Setites were always ridiculously united and the moment they started Embracing people outside of their religious paradigm, this was inevitable. I'm surprised it didn't happen centuries before.<br /> <br /> We finally have some diversity in the Ministry and good for them.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I fully admit my bias here because I played a Serpent of Light in my games who was heretical to the Followers of Set because he passionately believed in Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T12:03:24-07:00","id":1418684,"title":"","content":"Both the Serpents of Light and the &quot;Ministry&quot; are very heretic to be honest. SoL for previous reasons even before V5 because they were told not to join the Sabbat but did so anyway. Ministry because its way too western and like Philipps said, this far off group barely acknowledges Set wholesale as they usually should (all of a sudden.. throughout North America.. for some reason.. They also did the same exact thing that was a big no-no for the Serpents of Light- joining one of the Sects found in the West when they aren't supposed to). Further down the line I'd like so some supplement story with high-tier Setites head to the Americas on a campaign to clean house in the name of Set and ensure any possible Clan secrets in that timeframe... stay secrets again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T12:08:34-07:00","id":1418685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418684#post1418684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both the Serpents of Light and the &quot;Ministry&quot; are very heretic to be honest. SoL for previous reasons even before V5 because they were told not to join the Sabbat but did so anyway. Ministry because its way too western and like Philipps said, this far off group barely acknowledges Set wholesale as they usually should (all of a sudden.. throughout North America.. for some reason.. They also did the same exact thing that was a big no-no for the Serpents of Light- joining one of the Sects found in the West when they aren't supposed to). Further down the line I'd like so some supplement story with high-tier Setites head to the Americas on a campaign to clean house in the name of Set and ensure any possible Clan secrets in that timeframe... stay secrets again.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my remembrances of the 2nd Edition Followers of Set Clan Book and the Sabbat 2nd Edition Players Handbook, the Followers of Set went with their African followers to the Caribbean and set up blood cults with Ghede (another Baron Samedi clone) along with other FOS impersonating the Loa. The Followers of Set embraced a bunch of vampires in Haiti as the Sabbat spread through the New World. However, these Voodoo worshipers didn't take to the Followers of Set religion entirely and rebelled against what they perceived (correctly) as false gods. Now, the Followers of Set initially kicked their neonates asses but they joined with the Sabbat for some muscle.<br /> <br /> And the Followers of Set found themselves unable to do anything about the &quot;Serpents of Light&quot; even though joining the Sabbat was a lateral move evil wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T12:53:27-07:00","id":1418691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418682#post1418682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's called <b>Reality Ensues</b> to quote TVtropes.org.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, you want us to abandon our 3000 year old worship of Kali, THAT PREDATES SET and our culture to say she's a fragment of your god. One who wasn't EVIL IN THE FIRST PLACE in Egyptian mythology and venerate corruption? That's stupid. Your religion is stupid. Oh and you're stupid.&quot;<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Kali predates Set? Are you sure about that? From a cursory glance of Wikipedia, that ain't true at all. Like, Set was important around 3000bc. Kali maybe gets mentioned 1000bc but isn't a distinct 'God' till 600ad. <br /> <br /> I don't think it's 'reality ensues' at all. <br /> Set was supposedly benevolent at first but, y'know, most sick fucks pretend to be good people. perhaps his transition in perception could relate to his fall, as he was quite vilified much later on. <br /> Also, vampires tend to be better than average people, you want your clergy to know enough even if you want to trick the masses. The books before v5 gave us some reasonable logistics and.... <br /> <br /> How do I articulate this: Your idea of 'reality ensues' somehow lends itself to be the least realistic option. It's like if we had a look at a political spectrum, took the 5% of the radical left and the 5% of the radical right, and then applied them to 100% of the population. That's how V5's Ministry/Church appears. The other thing is, I was really, really sold on the followers and their middle-ground orthodoxy. The juicy deep philosophy has been gutted leaving only the parts that didn't actually fit in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T12:59:22-07:00","id":1418694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418691#post1418691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kali predates Set? Are you sure about that? From a cursory glance of Wikipedia, that ain't true at all. Like, Set was important around 3000bc. Kali maybe gets mentioned 1000bc but isn't a distinct 'God' till 600ad.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's 'reality ensues' at all.<br /> Set was supposedly benevolent at first but, y'know, most sick fucks pretend to be good people. perhaps his transition in perception could relate to his fall, as he was quite vilified much later on.<br /> Also, vampires tend to be better than average people, you want your clergy to know enough even if you want to trick the masses. The books before v5 gave us some reasonable logistics and....<br /> <br /> How do I articulate this: Your idea of 'reality ensues' somehow lends itself to be the least realistic option. It's like if we had a look at a political spectrum, took the 5% of the radical left and the 5% of the radical right, and then applied them to 100% of the population. That's how V5's Ministry/Church appears. The other thing is, I was really, really sold on the followers and their middle-ground orthodoxy. The juicy deep philosophy has been gutted leaving only the parts that didn't actually fit in...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, yeah, you disagree.<br /> <br /> But not my point at all.<br /> <br /> I don't think a clan without conflict makes any sense at all. The Followers of Set were all unified in their belief and cult which is nonsense for any religion. Schisms are inevitable as our local variants.<br /> <br /> The Church of Set had a reasonably good thing going ignoring the local variants for centuries but then in BJD (V20) that they started exterminating all who didn't acknowledge the Primacy and Eternity of Set Above All. Which drove the rest to form the Ministry. Fundamentalist variations of religions are a constant and these drove the rest away.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting this is a flaw, and I think this is what started the ball rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T13:40:22-07:00","id":1418700,"title":"","content":"Some various suggestions for fluff:<br /> <br /> * <b>Miami</b>, <b>San Salvador</b>, <b>Cape Town</b>, <b>Caracas</b>, and <b>Juarez/El Paso</b> are all Sabbat cities. Miami should be the capital of the American Sabbat but each of the Sabbat regions should have their own local leader.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Drowned</b> have taken huge chunks of South America and Central America but not all of it as it turned out plenty of local vampires prefer the Sabbat to centuries old pagan ones.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat have a large presence in <b>Istanbul</b> but are behaving because it's an Infernalist/Nephilim city. Mary the Black is the &quot;High Priestess&quot; of the city.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat are actually mostly in a state of truce with the <b>Ashirra</b> as they have bigger issues than the Muslim vampires.<br /> <br /> * The <b>Tzimisce</b> should have lost enough Elders to New York City, Blood Cults, Anarchs, and the Camarilla so that they're no longer a majority Clan either. As such, the Sabbat is now finally egalitarian in its treatment of <b>Antitribu</b>.<br /> <br /> * <b>Vykos</b> is the leader of the independent Tzimisce. They might return to become Regent of the Sabbat but are on a bit of a walkabout given their centuries of being under control of the Dracon and the knowledge the Eldest is Shub-Niggurath.<br /> <br /> * Drop the Antitribu line and they just identify by Clan now.<br /> <br /> * The <b>Serpents of Light</b> had a huge number of defections to the Ministry.<br /> <br /> * The <b>Loyalists</b> were weakened by many joining the Anarchs. Many Loyalists are unironically of the mind they're going to mold the Anarchs into a New Sabbat.<br /> <br /> * <b>Polonia</b> is Regent and he's operating out of <b>Dubai</b> where he has the Sabbat on their best behavior with the locals.<br /> <br /> * <b>Lucita</b> was regent for about a week and was overthrown by forces unknown. It was probably Marcus Vitel using Talley. She's missing presumed dead.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat have killed hundreds of Elders and a dozen or more Methuselahs in the <b>Gehenna War</b>. As nasty as the casualties are, they've done more damage to Elders and their masters than they have in the previous 600 years.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Seven Fires</b> are a breakaway Sabbat sect that are the purely evil mysterious terrorist Sabbat that have lost their minds. The Sabbat consider them traitors and extremists even by their standards but they're supported by others in the sect as well as &quot;not my problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> * The Revenant Families have either defected to join other powers, been Embraced, or have started passing themselves off as Thin Bloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T13:56:48-07:00","id":1418705,"title":"","content":"Why drop the Antitribu line, out of interest? Why cripple the Tzimisce? In short what upsides has the metaplot got for the Sabbat (and no the out break of suspension of disbelief shattering insanity called the gehena crusade is not an upside. It's the biggest pile of stupid since Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and just an excuse to buff the Anarchs.)<br /> <br /> Why would the Loyalists ever join the Anarchs? That is like a pro player joining a Sunday afternoon pub team.<br /> <br /> Regency makes sense, loosing ground to The Drowned, some one has to so ok (and hopefully that gives us another sect of inhuman vampires) SoL, ok makes some sense, but I don't have a large investment in the Setites so, Seven Fires need fleshing out properly before I can have an opinion either way.<br /> <br /> Revenant families are/were a Clan not sect resource, and should remain so.<br /> <br /> The rest should be a combination of damage limitation and soft retcon of the gehena crusade (because, again suddenly the Sabbat are stupider than a gi joe villian why?), Crusade to grab land that the Cam have abandoned, and generally kicking Anarchs out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-17-2020, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:09:14-07:00","id":1418709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418669#post1418669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, like, what do the serpents of the light actually believe in besides a rainbow serpent? Lightness and goodness? I recall reading they had a sunlight spell...<br /> <br /> Because they were heretical to the OG followers of Set that were far, far, far closer to &quot;the ministry&quot; than &quot;the church of set&quot;. So i think it pretty unlikely that they would join the ministry who should still be their enemies, but then again I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>when it comes to the serpents of the light &quot;cult&quot;, not much is known about their beliefs and ethics,<br /> however, the bloodline in general is pretty versatile religion wise, there are noddists among them, adherents to the cathari church etc<br /> <br /> also, not all of them are decended from the voodoo cult, some of them are followers or set that lost or cut ties with the main clan and defected to the sabbat (the sabbat bloodlines are always complicated like that)<br /> <br /> that doesn't matter anyway, what matters is that the serpents of the light were willing to join the sabbat to fight against the followers of set,<br /> since the ministry are bound to face hostilities with the followers of set at some point, I imagine the serpents of the light would be willing to ally with them even if they don't get along<br /> <br /> plus, both parties are sneaky manipulators, it doesn't have to be a friendly alliance, it could also be one group tricking the other<br /> <br /> it's kinda like the Brujah antitribu cooperating with anarch brujah on occasion against the camarilla (or even against the sabbat)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:20:32-07:00","id":1418710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418705#post1418705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why drop the Antitribu line, out of interest? Why cripple the Tzimisce? In short what upsides has the metaplot got for the Sabbat (and no the out break of suspension of disbelief shattering insanity called the gehena crusade is not an upside. It's the biggest pile of stupid since Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and just an excuse to buff the Anarchs.)<br /> <br /> Why would the Loyalists ever join the Anarchs? That is like a pro player joining a Sunday afternoon pub team.<br /> <br /> Regency makes sense, loosing ground to The Drowned, some one has to so ok (and hopefully that gives us another sect of inhuman vampires) SoL, ok makes some sense, but I don't have a large investment in the Setites so, Seven Fires need fleshing out properly before I can have an opinion either way.<br /> <br /> Revenant families are/were a Clan not sect resource, and should remain so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phipps is a novelist, and claims he's been playing since 1st ed,<br /> that would mean his fanfiction dates back to at least 20 years,<br /> don't be surprised if it deviates from yours \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af<br /> <br /> and revenant families have a history of betraying the Tzimisce and the sabbat,<br /> it will happen again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:23:46-07:00","id":1418711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418710#post1418710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Phipps is a novelist, and claims he's been playing since 1st ed,<br /> that would mean his fanfiction dates back to at least 20 years,<br /> don't be surprised if it deviates from yours \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af<br /> <br /> and revenant families have a history of betraying the Tzimisce and the sabbat,<br /> it will happen again</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, on the accidental and deliberate head canon.<br /> <br /> And fair the families do have a history of betrayal, but why now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:24:46-07:00","id":1418712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418694#post1418694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a clan without conflict makes any sense at all. The Followers of Set were all unified in their belief and cult which is nonsense for any religion. Schisms are inevitable as our local variants.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>See, you think we need a 'big schism' (ignoring SotL, but they're pretty small so..)<br /> <br /> But to me the Followers have always worked so well with small schisms and issues and unorthodoxy. Indian Setites? Quiet contention as they insist they're special and DON'T NEED YOU, DAD but also they practice beliefs that are entirely in line with the Settite paradigm so you can really kinda leave them alone. South American Settites? IS THAT PROTEAN?!? Are you sUrE you're not gAnGrEl with DELusions of GrandEUR? (Yeah they're all Gangrel with delusions of Grandeur) Scandinavian setites? Why don't you fuckers learn our magic since yours isn't fucking working? Bahari Setites? Yeah it works but I'm uncomftable with you making the manliest man to ever man into the first shitty wife? West African setites: I don't get <i>why </i>the clan's top dogs are apparently so cool with these guys. Their religion on the surface level seems so... thematically un-set like (but of course vampires can corrupt a 'nice' religion)<br /> Also if you're one of those crazy people that somehow thinks that the Witches of Echidna deserve to be cannon (They do not) you can have characters scream and rant and rave about how bullshit uneccessary they are.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Followers of Set are just a clusterfuck of &quot;does this cross the line?&quot; and that's great. You can totally have wars between setites over dogma and not fuck shit up for everyone. You can run chronicles of just trying to get settites onto the same page. If anything the ministry is really fucking stupid because the ministry should find even more enemies within the ministry than they would the Followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:24:55-07:00","id":1418714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418705#post1418705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why drop the Antitribu line, out of interest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it implies that the Brujah in the Sabbat are opposing the Brujah versus being the REAL Brujah in the first place. There's no need to establish them as an &quot;Anti-Clan&quot; in rebellion since the ones in the Sabbat are probably every bit as old, powerful, and &quot;real&quot; as the ones in other Clans. They're the REAL Clans versus anyone in Rebellion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why cripple the Tzimisce? </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking so the Tzimisce aren't stuck being the Sabbat's hand holder. The Sabbat will be at last the egalitarian organization of Kindred allied together they were always meant to be. The Tzimisce, Lasombra, and other Clans are all part of an alliance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short what upsides has the metaplot got for the Sabbat (and no the out break of suspension of disbelief shattering insanity called the gehena crusade is not an upside. It's the biggest pile of stupid since Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and just an excuse to buff the Anarchs.) </div> </div> </div>Honestly, having the Sabbat return home after having won the Gehenna Crusade is the best way to handle it. They've killed a good 10% of the vampires in the world and the majority of Camarilla Ancients. They won their war and now can work on new achievements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would the Loyalists ever join the Anarchs? That is like a pro player joining a Sunday afternoon pub team. </div> </div> </div>Because they are the best people fit to lead them and reform them from a nonfunctioning bunch of rabble to a new sect that will be truer to the Sabbat's principles of freedom.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if your argument begins, &quot;The Anarchs suck&quot; then it probably is best we drop that issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regency makes sense, loosing ground to The Drowned, some one has to so ok (and hopefully that gives us another sect of inhuman vampires) SoL, ok makes some sense, but I don't have a large investment in the Setites so, Seven Fires need fleshing out properly before I can have an opinion either way. </div> </div> </div>So noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revenant families are/were a Clan not sect resource, and should remain so. </div> </div> </div>This is notably not my idea. They'd begun a revolt against the Sabbat in BJD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rest should be a combination of damage limitation and soft retcon of the gehena crusade (because, again suddenly the Sabbat are stupider than a gi joe villian why?), Crusade to grab land that the Cam have abandoned, and generally kicking Anarchs out of the way. </div> </div> </div>Again, the Sabbat should win the Gehenna War and destroy the Camarilla ELders beckoned, adding their blood to the sect. Which is stated actually as happening in THE CAMARILLA.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla lost the Gehenna War to the Sabbat and now the majority of powerful Elders the Camarilla had are gone.<br /> <br /> FROM THE CAMARILLA, Page 181<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Some think the Sabbat weaker or less dangerous now that they have (seemingly) given up on controlling the cities of America and flocked to the war zones of the world, supposedly to revel freely in their vampiric nature under the cover of systematic bombings, atrocities, and the chaos of human warfare. I\u2019m sure they do, but that is not their purpose. These revenants, hardly Kindred at all, seek to transcend what it means to be human. They want to consume the eldest and wisest of us and infect all our species with their loss of self. This Gehenna war is not the end of them, it is another stage. It\u2019s a chrysalis. War is changing the Sabbat from the inside and out, and I dread what they will become, twisted and scarred by the fires of their victory. <b>I hate to be serious now, but you should know, whatever official reports are saying about the Gehenna war, we are not winning it.</b></span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:32:22-07:00","id":1418715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418710#post1418710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Phipps is a novelist, and claims he's been playing since 1st ed,<br /> that would mean his fanfiction dates back to at least 20 years,<br /> don't be surprised if it deviates from yours \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af<br /> <br /> and revenant families have a history of betraying the Tzimisce and the sabbat,<br /> it will happen again</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> Everyone's table is different in interpretations and readings of the material. The one constant is, &quot;The Storyteller is always right.&quot; This is more fanon than most, though, because we're speculating on how we could change the Sabbat when they come back from the Gehenna War and V5 finally gives us something to work with in the 3rd/2nd most popular sect in the setting. There's no wrong answers here and you could easily write a version where they conquer all of North America and establish the New Sabbat Empire.<br /> <br /> Just thought people would like a thread about house rules and possible ideas for reincorporating the Sword of Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:32:33-07:00","id":1418716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418711#post1418711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair, on the accidental and deliberate head canon.<br /> <br /> And fair the families do have a history of betrayal, but why now?</div> </div> </div> </div>this is a Fanon Thread, so...any reason you want (well, any reason HE wants)<br /> <br /> as far as canon goes, the Mexican Grimaldi have canonically planned a defection, but it was never mentioned if they succeeded or not (the lasombra defection would probably be a big help),<br /> <br /> I doubt the other families would plan to defect, but they might be forced to find refuge in other sects after the collapse of the sabbat and the SI onslaught<br /> <br /> best case scenario, they got embraced, or have moved along with the scattered sabbat cells and nomadic packs<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:36:52-07:00","id":1418717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418714#post1418714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it implies that the Brujah in the Sabbat are opposing the Brujah versus being the REAL Brujah in the first place. There's no need to establish them as an &amp;quot;Anti-Clan&amp;quot; in rebellion since the ones in the Sabbat are probably every bit as old, powerful, and &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; as the ones in other Clans. They're the REAL Clans versus anyone in Rebellion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking so the Tzimisce aren't stuck being the Sabbat's hand holder. The Sabbat will be at last the egalitarian organization of Kindred allied together they were always meant to be. The Tzimisce, Lasombra, and other Clans are all part of an alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, having the Sabbat return home after having won the Gehenna Crusade is the best way to handle it. They've killed a good 10% of the vampires in the world and the majority of Camarilla Ancients. They won their war and now can work on new achievements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because they are the best people fit to lead them and reform them from a nonfunctioning bunch of rabble to a new sect that will be truer to the Sabbat's principles of freedom.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if your argument begins, &amp;quot;The Anarchs suck&amp;quot; then it probably is best we drop that issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So noted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is notably not my idea. They'd begun a revolt against the Sabbat in BJD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, the Sabbat should win the Gehenna War and destroy the Camarilla ELders beckoned, adding their blood to the sect. Which is stated actually as happening in THE CAMARILLA.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla lost the Gehenna War to the Sabbat and now the majority of powerful Elders the Camarilla had are gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a very different view of the Anarchs it's true, mostly going back to my view of their treatment of real civil rights heroes as a WoD Gypsies level cock up, and the 'Shadowrunners with fangs' that became 'insulting pastiche of real political movements, but with added gang banging and fangs' as negatives I can't get past, with the majority of Anarchs players I have met just reinforcing that impression. So, yea I do have reasons for not liking them, but what ever.<br /> <br /> So ok, let them win the Crusade, drop the spirit nuke and pretend it was cleverer than it was originally portrayed as.<br /> <br /> Can't read BJD, the fonts make my dyspraxia (or rather the dyslexic side symptoms) go crazy, That has always been an issue I had to work around with weird don't choices, but BJD never goes to a readable font for me, so I have to read it over and over to get any meaning,, and doing that hurts, quite quickly.<br /> <br /> But my main sticking points (as you know) are Paths and Rites, and the treatment the cults get is not what I want for them, at all.<br /> <br /> On Antitribu, I always thought that was a declaration of opposition to the surviving Antediluvians, but, I guess your reasoning works as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:37:23-07:00","id":1418718,"title":"","content":"I should mention that the Sabbat are my second favorite sect after the Anarchs and I tend to think of the Camarilla as something that works best only when they're the bad guys. I've always enjoyed the contradictions of freedom/military/cult as well as the inhumanity of a sect when that will drive you to destruction yet feels more &quot;authentic&quot; to the vampire condition. I don't think that leaving them out of V5 was a wise decision even if I'm glad the Anarchs got the attention they finally deserved and sending them off to elsewhere is just silly for multiple reasons. Again, for the not inconsiderable reason that the Middle East is not Mordor, it's a real place and you can just call from a cellphone there or chat on Slack. ISIS is recruiting people over the internet from wartorn Syria and you can't tell me that someone can't figure out what the Sabbat is up to.<br /> <br /> So I'm definitely one of those people who want the Tzimisce in the Players Guide and a Sabbat book that should have been with the Anarchs and Camarilla books.<br /> <br /> I feel like the initial release of V5 and perhaps entire non-3rd party line should have been like this:<br /> <br /> * The Corebook<br /> * The Players Guide<br /> * The Anarchs<br /> * The Camarilla<br /> * The Sabbat<br /> * The Second Inquisition<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have a very different view of the Anarchs it's true, mostly going back to my view of their treatment of real civil rights heroes as a WoD Gypsies level cock up, and the 'Shadowrunners with fangs' that became 'insulting pastiche of real political movements, but with added gang banging and fangs' as negatives I can't get past, with the majority of Anarchs players I have met just reinforcing that impression. So, yea I do have reasons for not liking them, but what ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly understandable. For me, my love of Anarch boils down to the fact I'm a big fan of cyberpunk and the idea of a conflict between old powerful super-rich vampires versus poor &quot;street&quot; level gritty vampires. The &quot;punk&quot; element with vampirism replacing cybernetics and computers. Why are you fighting the Camarilla? Because you are the poor, young, and disenfranchised. Maybe you just want to be masters of the world yoursdelf or maybe you're a better person.<br /> For me, the Anarchs were always about the street vs. the ivory tower. I similarly love the Traditions vs. Technocracy for the same reason.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the Sabbat have a lot of this themselves so I have to emphasize their crazy self-destructive side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't read BJD, the fonts make my dyspraxia (or rather the dyslexic side symptoms) go crazy, That has always been an issue I had to work around with weird don't choices, but BJD never goes to a readable font for me, so I have to read it over and over to get any meaning,, and doing that hurts, quite quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, the Sabbat had some plotlines that haven't been followed up on yet:<br /> <br /> * The death of the Regent and a new Civil War with the various factions.<br /> <br /> * Lucita being supported by the Inquisition and Montreal for Regent.<br /> <br /> * Polonia claiming credit for 9/11 (wtf?) and wanting to invade the Middle East.<br /> <br /> * The Revenant Families planning a mass betrayal of the Sabbat because they felt they were superior beings to the vampires they've been carrying the asses of for the past 600 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T15:10:20-07:00","id":1418722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418718#post1418718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should mention that the Sabbat are my second favorite sect after the Anarchs and I tend to think of the Camarilla as something that works best only when they're the bad guys. I've always enjoyed the contradictions of freedom/military/cult as well as the inhumanity of a sect when that will drive you to destruction yet feels more &amp;quot;authentic&amp;quot; to the vampire condition. I don't think that leaving them out of V5 was a wise decision even if I'm glad the Anarchs got the attention they finally deserved and sending them off to elsewhere is just silly for multiple reasons. Again, for the not inconsiderable reason that the Middle East is not Mordor, it's a real place and you can just call from a cellphone there or chat on Slack. ISIS is recruiting people over the internet from wartorn Syria and you can't tell me that someone can't figure out what the Sabbat is up to.<br /> <br /> So I'm definitely one of those people who want the Tzimisce in the Players Guide and a Sabbat book that should have been with the Anarchs and Camarilla books.<br /> <br /> I feel like the initial release of V5 and perhaps entire non-3rd party line should have been like this:<br /> <br /> * The Corebook<br /> * The Players Guide<br /> * The Anarchs<br /> * The Camarilla<br /> * The Sabbat<br /> * The Second Inquisition<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Certainly understandable. For me, my love of Anarch boils down to the fact I'm a big fan of cyberpunk and the idea of a conflict between old powerful super-rich vampires versus poor &amp;quot;street&amp;quot; level gritty vampires. The &amp;quot;punk&amp;quot; element with vampirism replacing cybernetics and computers. Why are you fighting the Camarilla? Because you are the poor, young, and disenfranchised. Maybe you just want to be masters of the world yoursdelf or maybe you're a better person.<br /> For me, the Anarchs were always about the street vs. the ivory tower. I similarly love the Traditions vs. Technocracy for the same reason.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the Sabbat have a lot of this themselves so I have to emphasize their crazy self-destructive side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, well, the Sabbat had some plotlines that haven't been followed up on yet:<br /> <br /> * The death of the Regent and a new Civil War with the various factions.<br /> <br /> * Lucita being supported by the Inquisition and Montreal for Regent.<br /> <br /> * Polonia claiming credit for 9/11 (wtf?) and wanting to invade the Middle East.<br /> <br /> * The Revenant Families planning a mass betrayal of the Sabbat because they felt they were superior beings to the vampires they've been carrying the asses of for the past 600 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the bullet points.<br /> <br /> On Cyberpunk, I like it as a genre as well, but the Anarchs never hit that vibe for me.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat however hit the successful revolutionary paramilitary organization vibe, with added mysticism and totally inhuman monstrosity, combining things I find fascinating from modern history with what I love about schlock b movie vampire horror, with a dash of occultism, I was and am hooked, but then I always liked Necroscope, Dusk til Dawn, and 30 Days of Night more than Anne Rice. That ability to be a combination of Che Guevara, Crowley and the Lovecraftian Horror of Viscutitude and Obtenebration was to good to miss (but that Cosmic Horror is gone now, with Viscutitude just being weird Protean, and Obtenebration now a type of necromancy...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />..)...<br /> <br /> This wall of text brings me to my point: The Sabbat as a revolutionary occult movement, combining Maoist and Leninist military tactics, with initiation and mystery cult aspects, with the conflict between the Paths and philosophies being it's main weakness, but also it's dynamism. So Nomadic Packs as Maoist style infiltration units and evangelical recruiters, Covens as Guards units and the strength of the main force, the Inquisition as Commissars, the Black Hand as combination special forces, religious order, and secret police. You end up with a totalitarian nightmare waiting to happen preaching freedom, enlightenment and revolutionary justice...and being right, because no one said the world was nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T15:32:21-07:00","id":1418724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418722#post1418722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the bullet points.<br /> <br /> On Cyberpunk, I like it as a genre as well, but the Anarchs never hit that vibe for me.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat however hit the successful revolutionary paramilitary organization vibe, with added mysticism and totally inhuman monstrosity, combining things I find fascinating from modern history with what I love about schlock b movie vampire horror, with a dash of occultism, I was and am hooked, but then I always liked Necroscope, Dusk til Dawn, and 30 Days of Night more than Anne Rice. That ability to be a combination of Che Guevara, Crowley and the Lovecraftian Horror of Viscutitude and Obtenebration was to good to miss (but that Cosmic Horror is gone now, with Viscutitude just being weird Protean, and Obtenebration now a type of necromancy...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />..)...<br /> <br /> This wall of text brings me to my point: The Sabbat as a revolutionary occult movement, combining Maoist and Leninist military tactics, with initiation and mystery cult aspects, with the conflict between the Paths and philosophies being it's main weakness, but also it's dynamism. So Nomadic Packs as Maoist style infiltration units and evangelical recruiters, Covens as Guards units and the strength of the main force, the Inquisition as Commissars, the Black Hand as combination special forces, religious order, and secret police. You end up with a totalitarian nightmare waiting to happen preaching freedom, enlightenment and revolutionary justice...and being right, because no one said the world was nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very notable,<br /> <br /> For me, the Anarchs occupy the role of the &quot;urban resistance&quot; that does draw elements from real life social movements but it doesn't replace them or control them. In the original 1st Edition Chicago by Night, one of the subtler things about the Anarchs was the generational divide between the 1920s Socialist Unionists (Tarponski), the 70s Civil Rights Era activists (Anita Blake, Maldavis), and the modern day Punks (Gengis, Damien, Evelyn Stephens)<br /> <br /> The Anarchs should always include idealists among them but also people trying to take advantage of that idealism and people are just the criminals of the Camarilla. The Camarilla is the Godfather and Michael Corleone while the Anarchs are the street level thugs and deals.<br /> <br /> With the Sabbat, I generally think of them as, &quot;Just a reminder these are the REAL vampires.&quot; V:TM is awesome and I do love the Louis, Angel, Forever Knight, and &quot;Oh woe is me, I am damned vampires.&quot; However, vampire stories started with them as horrifying evil monsters. Dracula, Carmilla, Ruthven, and Nosferatu. The Sabbat fills a role in the setting that the Humanity rules kind of prevent from happening that there definitely needs to be vampires who rejoice in their evil as well as destroying lives. The Sabbat may go over the top but as you mentioned, the Necroscope and Buffy vampires are in need of someonew who can represent them too.<br /> <br /> Without the Sabbat, you don't have anyone who can (with a straight face) say THE SATANIC RITES OF DRACULA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eMAgmFScQvU\" data-code=\"eMAgmFScQvU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eMAgmFScQvU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I feel like V:TM is a lesser setting without the Sabbat because the whole &quot;fight for your humanity&quot; business loses significant edge if you don't have someone who represents the Far End of What You Can BecomeTM if you're playing Camarilla or Anarch and if you're playing Sabbat then you can go areas where you normally wouldn't like alien cults, rituals, and more. It's still a horror game but the question is not, &quot;can you be good?&quot; but &quot;How far are you willing to go even after you're damned?&quot;<br /> <br /> In the original UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON, one of the best moments is in the Sabbat campaign when <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Phillipe Rigaud orders your pack to Embrace a bunch of Werewolf Kinfolk and Dominate them into eating the rest of their family, including a baby (or Embrace the children to eat their parents).<br /> <br /> It's pointlessly sadistic and evil and designed just to piss the werewolves off. However, some of the Paths would actually object to that and perhaps even cause some to wonder at their Humanity's loss. I feel it's a great scene for the kind of horror that vampires can do. Mind you, I also hated when they got rid of the Path of Harmony as it meant that the one &quot;decent-ish&quot; group in the Sabbat was gone and thus not there to reign it all back.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2020, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T15:34:59-07:00","id":1418726,"title":"","content":"I never liked the Anarchs due to the day/night cycle,<br /> I don't get the whole &quot;punk&quot; thing they had going on,<br /> <br /> the contrast in the image of a rebel freedom fighter punk having an assortment of ghouls to groom them doesn't sit right with me<br /> <br /> I like the sabbat imagery better, mostly the one of the communal haven, the sabbat nest devoted to the night and abusing mortals,<br /> to me they fit better as rebel monsters,<br /> <br /> though they still need some better mechanics to support their bullshit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-19-2020, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T16:06:35-07:00","id":1418730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418724#post1418724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very notable,<br /> <br /> For me, the Anarchs occupy the role of the &quot;urban resistance&quot; that does draw elements from real life social movements but it doesn't replace them or control them. In the original 1st Edition Chicago by Night, one of the subtler things about the Anarchs was the generational divide between the 1920s Socialist Unionists (Tarponski), the 70s Civil Rights Era activists (Anita Blake, Maldavis), and the modern day Punks (Gengis, Damien, Evelyn Stephens)<br /> <br /> The Anarchs should always include idealists among them but also people trying to take advantage of that idealism and people are just the criminals of the Camarilla. The Camarilla is the Godfather and Michael Corleone while the Anarchs are the street level thugs and deals.<br /> <br /> With the Sabbat, I generally think of them as, &quot;Just a reminder these are the REAL vampires.&quot; V:TM is awesome and I do love the Louis, Angel, Forever Knight, and &quot;Oh woe is me, I am damned vampires.&quot; However, vampire stories started with them as horrifying evil monsters. Dracula, Carmilla, Ruthven, and Nosferatu. The Sabbat fills a role in the setting that the Humanity rules kind of prevent from happening that there definitely needs to be vampires who rejoice in their evil as well as destroying lives. The Sabbat may go over the top but as you mentioned, the Necroscope and Buffy vampires are in need of someonew who can represent them too.<br /> <br /> Without the Sabbat, you don't have anyone who can (with a straight face) say THE SATANIC RITES OF DRACULA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eMAgmFScQvU\" data-code=\"eMAgmFScQvU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eMAgmFScQvU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I feel like V:TM is a lesser setting without the Sabbat because the whole &quot;fight for your humanity&quot; business loses significant edge if you don't have someone who represents the Far End of What You Can BecomeTM if you're playing Camarilla or Anarch and if you're playing Sabbat then you can go areas where you normally wouldn't like alien cults, rituals, and more. It's still a horror game but the question is not, &quot;can you be good?&quot; but &quot;How far are you willing to go even after you're damned?&quot;<br /> <br /> In the original UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON, one of the best moments is in the Sabbat campaign when <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Phillipe Rigaud orders your pack to Embrace a bunch of Werewolf Kinfolk and Dominate them into eating the rest of their family, including a baby (or Embrace the children to eat their parents).<br /> <br /> It's pointlessly sadistic and evil and designed just to piss the werewolves off. However, some of the Paths would actually object to that and perhaps even cause some to wonder at their Humanity's loss. I feel it's a great scene for the kind of horror that vampires can do. Mind you, I also hated when they got rid of the Path of Harmony as it meant that the one &quot;decent-ish&quot; group in the Sabbat was gone and thus not there to reign it all back.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Loosing Harmony for Feral Heart did suck (or that weird dualist Montreal path whose name escapes me), The Sabbat should be this alliance of licks who hate the antes and cast aside humanity, the purges come after you win, not during the war, the settling of accounts and ossification of faith to religion happens when and where peace and power are secure, with that comes a new kind of horror. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat, or rather the Paths should be where you end up, with Humanity impossible to hold in the long term, as the few decades of life are swamped by centuries of undeath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T16:44:15-07:00","id":1418735,"title":"","content":"Love the Hammer film trailer. <br /> <br /> Sabbath have always been my favorite, ever since they came out with that book for them back in the early 90's. I liked the cleaning Paths got in revised, did not like that most were on Humanity. I like the flexible system of morality that (unfortunately) V5 labelled Humanity. But I digress...<br /> <br /> Piggy-backing on the whole #winningGehennaWar, I think I could see an interesting take on the bogey-man aspect. The Sabbat comes back, and they begin hunting down the Monty Coven vampires (ones taken over by Diablerie), starting with their own. In a total surprise move no one thought, the Inquisition and Black Hand team up for this. Remnants of the Tal Mahe Ra could try to use it to their advantage, steering Packs toward targets they want eliminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T16:49:16-07:00","id":1418736,"title":"","content":"I love the Path of Harmony, but in a way made sense. It also could provide a great jumping point for the Anarch defectors. 'Yeah, sure, we're all freedom blah blah blah. Till ya try to tell yer packmate maybe slitting throats just because isn't a great plan. Suddenly, yer a traitor to the cause. Well, we were the original Anarchs, maybe it's time to get back to our roots.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T18:11:36-07:00","id":1418745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418726#post1418726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked the Anarchs due to the day/night cycle,<br /> <br /> I don't get the whole &quot;punk&quot; thing they had going on,</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit this is my games but I remember MARK REIN HAGEN's take on Gary very implicitly and that's always influenced my views of the extremes of vampiredom. Specifically, my view of the World of Darkness is very &quot;dirty.&quot; I mean that literally, when I describe the cities of the WOD I always try and think of 70s New York. The place is covered in trash, there's newspapers all around, the air is filthy, and it is crumbling unless it's brand new.<br /> <br /> This applies to the Anarchs vs. Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is rich, powerful, decadent, and living in ivory towers and beautiful decaying manners with literal slaves that have been with them for centuries. They're the 1% of Kindredom, maybe 10% if we're being generous because Toreador and Ventrue tend to be rich no matter what.<br /> <br /> The other 90%? They're living in abandoned factories, squatting in condemned houses, living in the basement of apartment buildings in closets. They're hunting night to night for their own survival. Poor vampires are a thing and survival is a struggle.<br /> <br /> I feel that makes the conflict between Camarilla and Anarchs very clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the contrast in the image of a rebel freedom fighter punk having an assortment of ghouls to groom them doesn't sit right with me </div> </div> </div>I had the view that Anarchs who have ghouls fall into a number of different views:<br /> <br /> 1. An Anarch views a ghoul as a trusted friend and retainer who just happens to be Blood Bound. Inevitably, the blood will destroy their friendship but that is actually part of the tragedy.<br /> <br /> 2. An Anarch will choose not to have ghouls as servants period and thus actually weaken their protection during the day.<br /> <br /> 3. An Anarch will be a crime boss who employs henchmen as ghouls and thinks nothing of it because he's in it for the $$$.<br /> <br /> 4. An Anarch, unlike WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS, will Embrace their ghoul servant if they survive 4, 6, or 10 years of service.<br /> <br /> 5. They're mortals so fuck em. Vampires have rights, humans don't because Anarchs are hypocrites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T19:11:13-07:00","id":1418752,"title":"","content":"Something else I'd do with the Sabbat is blend with the Baali. With the Gehenna War, I see Sabbat Packs destroying/taken over/corrupted by Baali Nests in the Middle East. These Sabbat will be like the Molochim and Nergali Baali, with the twist of believing the Sleepers are ancient, possibly Antediluvian, vampires. So, some will be seeking to keep them asleep (because destroying them isn't working), others to serve them (if you can't beat them, join them).<br /> <br /> I'd tie this in with the Black Hand/Inquisition team up too (enemy of my enemy...) In summary, the V5 Sabbat would be as follows:<br /> <br /> - Anarch defectors (Sabbat that truly believe in the freedom from tyrannical Elders and the viciousness to do what Anarchs can't or won't)<br /> - Returning Gehenna Crusaders (Sabbat trying to find meaning to unlife after war)<br /> - Those That Stayed Behind/Ignored the War (Sabbat trying to keep what little territory they have)<br /> - Black Hand/Inquisition cells (What more need be said?)<br /> - Corrupted Sabbat (Sabbat That are everything from Satanic to Lovecraftian)<br /> <br /> With no Regent in place, the Sabbat is decentralized. Sure, the Black Hand and Inquisition may try to be putting some semblance of order together, but right now, you could wipe out a whole city of them and the Sect will not come tumbling down. With no center of authority, the Sabbat is now everywhere and nowhere. Aside from a few remaining cities, the majority of Sabbat are nomadic.<br /> <br /> This, and the attention of SI, is what necessitated trimming down Ritae.<br /> <br /> The Gehenna War and Lasombra defection is what brought back the Pack Embrace and elevation of the Ignoblis Ritae One of My Tribe to Auctoritas (can't be Beckoned if you have no Clan to call you).<br /> <br /> The Baali may have been a Clan, may have been a bloodline, may have been a cult. Thanks to the Gehenna War, their practices will be carried on.<br /> <br /> I'm enjoying this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T20:55:58-07:00","id":1418761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418730#post1418730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loosing Harmony for Feral Heart did suck (or that weird dualist Montreal path whose name escapes me),...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nocturnal Redemption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T21:25:45-07:00","id":1418766,"title":"","content":"In any case, I think the Sabbat &quot;winning&quot; the Gehenna War (albeit without destroying the Antediluvians) is better than the chump-end of marching off to be eaten by the Ancients.<br /> <br /> It nicely gets rid of a lot of Camarilla Elders and frees up many places for PCs to take their place but it doesn't make the Sabbat look like they are a bunch of morons either.<br /> <br /> <b>How some fans see the Gehenna Crusade</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mLyOj_QD4a4\" data-code=\"mLyOj_QD4a4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mLyOj_QD4a4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-18-2020, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T23:18:11-07:00","id":1418774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418761#post1418761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nocturnal Redemption?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the one. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T03:14:27-07:00","id":1418790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418766#post1418766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, I think the Sabbat &quot;winning&quot; the Gehenna War (albeit without destroying the Antediluvians) is better than the chump-end of marching off to be eaten by the Ancients.<br /> <br /> It nicely gets rid of a lot of Camarilla Elders and frees up many places for PCs to take their place but it doesn't make the Sabbat look like they are a bunch of morons either.<br /> <br /> <b>How some fans see the Gehenna Crusade</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mLyOj_QD4a4\" data-code=\"mLyOj_QD4a4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mLyOj_QD4a4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>More like <a href=\"https://youtu.be/k3sRzY_RXDk?t=165\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/k3sRzY_RXDk?t=165</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T08:25:46-07:00","id":1418828,"title":"","content":"Some quick thoughts on a V5 Sabbat in light of the events in BJD and the V5 Books.<br /> <br /> Sabbat realigned along lines similar to Crusader Orders led by charismatic individuals such as Polonia, Lucita and Dracula, retaining pack and path affiliations but allowing for a more regional variation and outlook.<br /> <br /> Path\u2019s to be reintroduced \u2013 characters are free to create tenets to reflect this, but each Path to have \u2018Ideal\u2019 Tenets illustrated \u2013 this would reflect the divergence from Humanity, and the fact that the Vampire is basically following and forging a morality code which is not hardwired into them like humanity is supposed to be. They could be written as the personal tenets of those who came before, and passed down to fellow adherents. <br /> <br /> In the same way Touchstones do need to reflect the altered morality \u2013 they might be human, but they could be a collection of fragments from the Book of Nod which the character turns to in times of crisis, or the shared Ritae of their Pack to renew their faith and purpose. <br /> <br /> V5 changes to Tzmisce: Gaining Blood Sorcery for Vicissitude. Blood powers go to the Path of Blood and Fleshcraft/Bonecraft/Zulo to be rituals. This would reflect their Dracula/Necroscopic origin \u2013 based on a line in the Chicago Folios. <br /> <br /> V5 Changes to Ravnos: Become an accepted clan of the Sabbat as the largest faction is there. They use a form of Obfuscate to create illusion and misdirection. Their Bane would be a variation of the Requiem Nosferatu, appearing \u2018wrong\u2019 impacting their interaction with others, notably mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>I'm God's hated messenger, the Devil's cohort<br /> I'm the one they all blame, when a life is cut short<br /> But still if you're willing, to give it a try<br /> I'll beat you at anything, and claim you're last sigh</i><br /> - The Reaper's Tales","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4688-malkira","name":"Malkira","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T09:00:58-07:00","id":1418833,"title":"","content":"*calms himself down*<br /> <br /> Changing Vicissitude to sorcery isn't half as stupid as merging it into Protean. Rituals make too-much sense in terms of recreating the intricate and lengthly surgeries you'll be doing. (I have a Vicissitude 'procedure' list written down in my own brew) and Sorcery thematically and narratively fits it much, much, much better than Protean. Oh, and it would bring the old-clan a little closer to the new<br /> <br /> All that said. <br /> Vicissitude works best as Vicissitude, mergers cause more problems than they solve, and I get a deep, emotional scare everytime someone comes up with a 'good idea' for subsuming vicissitude into some other power. I also think it would do a diservice to blood sorcerers since it disregards paradigm and makes you wonder why Tremere and assamites don't... oh what am I saying, <i>everything</i> does a disservice to blood sorcerers in V5. Vampire sorcerers are the red headed step child that deserves the beating they get for thinking they can aspire to greater things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T09:29:47-07:00","id":1418841,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I agree. It's illogical to put Vicissitude in Blood Sorcery because Vicissitude is a physical based discipline specified toward altering Flesh and Bone. It's not sorcery but something of primordial viscera. Also another point I agree with from MWIS is the weird thing about everyone always clamoring for Vicissitude to be clobbered into some other discipline... what's up with that? Do people who actually like the Tzimisce legitimately suggest stuff like that? lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:04:47-07:00","id":1418846,"title":"","content":"Another thing that bothers me is that Viscissitude is a product of the body, some people fear it as a disease. <br /> <br /> Though v5 clearly does not agree, Thaumaturgy is a product of the soul. It is not unique to vampires. mortals may practice it. Lupines may practice it. I don't know about changelings but I suspect wraiths cannot. Vitae just makes things more convenient, but it is an entirely foreign thing to the Beast. Which is why it cannot be used in frenzy for 4 editions (much of this applies to necromancy: Quietus and Obtenebration obviously were normal disciplines that worked in frenzy)<br /> <br /> So, from the perspective of someone who got invested in the game before v5, It's mighty weird to have Vicissitude, a very... fleshy Discipline, to become a sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:15:14-07:00","id":1418851,"title":"","content":"For my games I usually take a kind of 20.5 tack as I\u2019ve explained on this server before, but as I return from college business, I\u2019ll try to elaborate upon that and say how I tend to handle the Sabbat in those instances. Hopefully people enjoy and find some inspiration in it.<br /> <br /> So in 2004, after the ups-and-downs of the East Coast Crusades, the Red Star caused what may have been a near miss with a Gehenna. It\u2019s a mystery and no one knows for sure. Regardless, it certainly caused a stir in vampiric society.<br /> <br /> New York City had fallen and the Sabbat was scrambling to cover their pride and respond to the dark portents around them. The factions grew more and more divided as a result of this and the fuse of the Fourth Sabbat Civil War was becoming primed.<br /> <br /> The Ultra-Conservatives in Europe were still stagnant, the Conservatives in the Americas were wary of the loss of key assets, but the most dangerous were the Loyalists. Not only were Panders and their Loyalist allies pandering for a less rigid hierarchy, The Gehenna Prophetess had raised a call for a crusade into the Holy Lands and hordes of Sabbat were answering.<br /> <br /> The Status Quo bloc struggled to keep their rank and file orderly while also having to show support for the Gehenna Crusade or risk further insurrection or even retribution from Gehenna Crusaders. The Old World and the New saw ideologues flocking to the Crusade, exasperating the plight of wightdom within the Sabbat\u2019s ranks as domains had even fewer Enlightened to indoctrinate new recruits away from Humanitas.<br /> <br /> Whenever the final death of the regent becomes known, the Fourth Sabbat Civil War became unpreventable. Giangaleazzo watched the mayhem and heard the worrying reports of shadows waking in old Mediterranean tombs and decided to cash out alongside a generation of Status Quo Lasombra who were either disillusioned, unwilling to crusade, unwilling to risk their hides in Civil War, or thought the Status Quo &amp; Hyper-Conservative factions were loosing too much power and influence.<br /> <br /> This movement alongside an influx of Gangrel &amp; Salubri, and exit of many Assamites &amp; Harbingers; the destruction of so many Goratrix Tremere, this all led to catastrophic results within the sects ranks. The Black Hand was gutted by the losses and struggling to recoup while the Inquisition furthered the chaos by going on a frenzy of investigations against both over-zealous Loyalists and under-zealous Status Quo. Those calling for the Prophestess to be declared a heretic caused even more tension, bloodshed, and monomancy.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat is not gone. Historically, the Sabbat rises from each Civil War stronger, reborn in the crucible. Yet this may be different. Never has the fighting been so vast and upon such sharp ideological lines. The revolt of the Loyalists leads many Conservatives to resist attempts of reconciliation until they are brought to heel and the treason of the Lasombra and so many Conservatives leads many Loyalists to howl for the heart\u2019s blood of all the non-believers in the sect\u2019s ranks.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat struggles to maintain its prominence along the North American Coastlines, throughout Central &amp; South America, across war-then regions of sub-Saharan Africa and the Middle East, and their old holdings in Mediterranean and Eastern Europe. <br /> <br /> The battle is fierce though and will occupy every level of the midnight society until its complete. Perhaps the PC\u2019s will play a key role in shifting the balance of their domain in their faction\u2019s favor though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T11:45:49-07:00","id":1418868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418846#post1418846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that bothers me is that Viscissitude is a product of the body, some people fear it as a disease.<br /> <br /> Though v5 clearly does not agree, Thaumaturgy is a product of the soul. It is not unique to vampires. mortals may practice it. Lupines may practice it. I don't know about changelings but I suspect wraiths cannot. Vitae just makes things more convenient, but it is an entirely foreign thing to the Beast. Which is why it cannot be used in frenzy for 4 editions (much of this applies to necromancy: Quietus and Obtenebration obviously were normal disciplines that worked in frenzy)<br /> <br /> So, from the perspective of someone who got invested in the game before v5, It's mighty weird to have Vicissitude, a very... fleshy Discipline, to become a sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics wise, I always felt that Vicissitude was just flat out overpowered as its problem. So making it either Protean OR Blood Sorcery is a mistake.<br /> <br /> How I would do it is make its power to affect others a combo discipline.<br /> <br /> Here's how it would work:<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce get <b>Animalism, Protean, and Blood Sorcery</b>. They get thus the full <b>Dracula Combo</b> that simulate the vast majority of his traditional powers.<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce Protean allows them to shapeshift THEMSELVES into wolves, bats, Zulo form, claws, and changing their appearance with Fleshcraft or Bonecraft.<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce Protean /Blood Sorcery would allow them to Fleshcraft OTHERS with surgeries and their labs on a permanent basis.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce would thus still have one of the most powerful Disciplines and combos in the entire game but not outrageously so.<br /> <br /> As for Thaumaturgy, I should note I have a much more &quot;crunch&quot; based view of magic.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't teach their magic to ghouls or mortals or werewolves. They draw their quintessence for their spells from the blood that is provided to them via a quintessence processing machine (i.e. the vampire themselves). Vampire blood is magical and thus can power magic. Hedge magic requires another source of magic via spirit, rituals, or sacrifices. True magic uses the avatar and drains it from the universe.<br /> <br /> It's a complicated non-instinctual process unlike Frenzy, so why you don't see Wights using it or other high level disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-18-2020, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T12:10:39-07:00","id":1418871,"title":"","content":"I understand that some want Vicissitude to be Vicissitude. I can appreciate that.<br /> I based my suggestions on answering the OP of bringing the Sabbat to V5, which seems to be following a policy of pruning Disciplines &amp; Bloodlines in favour of individually tailored power-sets within fewer Disciplines.<br /> For Vicissitude, Protean seems a great fit at first, but that wouldn't cover the Tzmisce's command of Blood, Flesh and Bone sufficiently for me. Also if we were to try the reduce Disciplines &amp; Bloodlines then Koldunism is either out altogether or so warped it no longer serves its purpose. By adding Blood Sorcery to the Tzmisce I imagine a discipline which allows Koldun's &amp; Vicissitude practioners to sit within the same power set (No it isnt perfect, but this is an idea based on the change being inevitable - if that wasnt the case then I would keep the two bloodlines)<br /> I also thought about Vicissitude being a Path of Blood Sorcery (The Path of Flesh &amp; Bone? The Way of Vicissitude?) but I have no evidence there will ever be more than one Path in Blood Sorcery. so I proceeded accordingly.<br /> Also as mentioned in adding Vicissitude to Blood Sorcery I think it draws the Old &amp; New Clan closer - You need your Translyvanian Count to skitter headfirst down a wall like a spider? There's already a ritual for that.<br /> I also sort of assumed that Blood Sorcery was not Thaumaturgy (though Thaumaturgy is part of Blood Sorcery) It was a catch-all category which represents the core principle of 'Vampire Magic' within the game. Your average Tzmisce Koldun, Tremere Thaumaturge or Banu Haquim Sorcerer might not see themselves the same. But from a game perspective I dont mind all my Rituals in one place where, as GM, I can say 'The Fleshcrafting Ritual is a speciality of the Tzmisce, as a Banu Haquim Sorcerer you need a Tzmisce Mentor before you can even think about learning that'<br /> <br /> Just thought I would lay out my thinking.<br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>I'm God's hated messenger, the Devil's cohort<br /> I'm the one they all blame, when a life is cut short<br /> But still if you're willing, to give it a try<br /> I'll beat you at anything, and claim you're last sigh</i><br /> - The Reaper's Tales","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4688-malkira","name":"Malkira","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T12:21:02-07:00","id":1418872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Tzimisce get <b>Animalism, Protean, and Blood Sorcery</b>. They get thus the full <b>Dracula Combo</b> that simulate the vast majority of his traditional powers.<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce Protean allows them to shapeshift THEMSELVES into wolves, bats, Zulo form, claws, and changing their appearance with Fleshcraft or Bonecraft.<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce Protean /Blood Sorcery would allow them to Fleshcraft OTHERS with surgeries and their labs on a permanent basis.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce would thus still have one of the most powerful Disciplines and combos in the entire game but not outrageously so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still fail to see what exactly is &quot;outrageous&quot; about Vicissitude whatsoever. Its very average and only gets &quot;overpowered&quot; past its 5 mark, but that's the case with all Disciplines past said mark.. ergo &quot;Elder Disciplines.&quot; Also again, Tzimisce are based off of and take from alot of things. There is no reason that should just be pigeon-holed to just some &quot;Dracula&quot; trope or whatever combo you reference at all. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> said before and a sentiment I also share, Vicissitude is Vicissitude, not Animalism (Tzimisce already have this, why mention it?), Protean, or Blood Sorcery. No fan of the Tzimisce wants a change to Vicissitude whatsoever. If you want Tzimisce that specialize in Blood Magic, look for the variant Old Clan Tzimisce or just work your way up to be a Koldun, but there is no logical meta reason for Tzimisice to have their signature Discipline canned for the aforementioned replacement Disciplines.<br /> <br /> But you know however, seeing what happened with the Lasombra and the canning of Obtenebration for the illogical mismash with Necromancy to form &quot;Oblivion,&quot; whenever we do see the Tzimisce again in V5 they'd probably scrap Vicissitude with some excuse anyway AND replace it with Protean as sermon'd by some people around here. They already jacked Serpentis for Protean for whatever reason (and before any replies come certaining this - no, just because a certain Discipline as to do with changing physical form doesn't mean it needs to be hammered into Protean mindlessly. Serpentis was COMPLETELY different from Protean from a mechanical, meta, and lore-aspectation but still was shoved in).<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkira</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also as mentioned in adding Vicissitude to Blood Sorcery I think it draws the Old &amp; New Clan closer</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, Blood Sorcery is based on Rituals- in another thread concerning this, I touched on this: Rituals are an ACTIVE process you have to attend to with multiple steps and focused knowledge. Vicissitude is a force of nature and an instinct to one who knows the Discipline. It is no shape-or-form a ritualized ability in the same length of Blood Sorcery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-18-2020, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T12:24:55-07:00","id":1418873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418872#post1418872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still fail to see what exactly is &quot;outrageous&quot; about Vicissitude whatsoever. Its very average and only gets &quot;overpowered&quot; past its 5 mark, but that's the case with all Disciplines past said mark.. ergo &quot;Elder Disciplines.&quot; Also again, Tzimisce are based off of and take from alot of things. There is no reason that should just be pigeon-holed to just some &quot;Dracula&quot; trope or whatever combo you reference at all. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> said before and a sentiment I also share, Vicissitude is Vicissitude, not Animalism (Tzimisce already have this, why mention it?), Protean, or Blood Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animalism would have no role in Vicissitude. It would just be listing their three Disciplines. I think Blood Sorcery fits the Tzimisce better than Auspex. Because when I think of the ancient lords of the land and traditionalist vampires, I think of Anne Rice Psychic Powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No fan of the Tzimisce wants a change to Vicissitude whatsoever. </div> </div> </div>That's stupid because I am a HUGE Tzimisce fan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want Tzimisce that specialize in Blood Magic, look for the variant Old Clan Tzimisce or just work your way up to be a Koldun, but there is no logical meta reason for Tzimisice to have their signature Discipline canned for the aforementioned replacement Disciplines. </div> </div> </div>Any *REAL* Tzimisce fan loves them as sorcerers and mad scientists. No one should want them to be a bunch of flesh crafting losers without magic or their own labs. That's not a Tzimisce. That's a poseur. Dudes who just go around morphing faces defile the sacred power of the Eldest.<br /> <br /> A real Tzimisce should also seek Koldunism because that's their birthright and sacred power to master their connection with the land.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you know however, seeing what happened with the Lasombra and the canning of Obtenebration for the illogical mismash with Necromancy to form &quot;Oblivion,&quot; whenever we do see the Tzimisce again in V5 they'd probably scrap Vicissitude with some excuse anyway AND replace it with Protean as sermon'd by some people around here. </div> </div> </div>Because Protean is awesome. It needs a power up, though, because shapeshifting should be more versatile than just wolves and bats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They already jacked Serpentis for Protean for whatever reason (and before any replies come certaining this - no, just because a certain Discipline as to do with changing physical form doesn't mean it needs to be hammered into Protean mindlessly. Serpentis was COMPLETELY different from Protean from a mechanical, meta, and lore-aspectation but still was shoved in). </div> </div> </div>Yes, because Serpentis was a joke discipline. They made it actually worthwhile.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Sadly, I feel they ruined the Old Clan Tzimisce or perhaps they made the regular Clan Tzimisce more interesting. The Eldest has Vicissitude and the oldest and most powerful of Tzimisce also have Vicissitude like Yorak. Therefore, there's no point in having Old Clan Tzimisce because Vicissitude is their signature Discipline. Thankfully, since the Old Clan were always 900% more cooler than the regular Clan, merging the two and just forgetting there was any schism over Disciplines in the first place benefits the Tzimisce as a whole.<br /> <br /> Castles, estates, ghouled servants, and weird experiments FTW.<br /> <br /> I will say we've had this argument before but its clear that a lot of people have different ideas on what the Tzimisce SHOULD BE. For me, they are the Clan of not just Dracula but Doctor Frankenstein, Pinhead, mad science, demonic sorcery, Doctor Frank N. Furter, Doctor Giggles, and other creepy B-movie &quot;smart guys are evil.&quot; There's the occasional Tzimisce Surgeon with the Path of Harmony or even Nocturnal Redemption who heals with Vicissitude but they should all be super-duper smart people that are pressing the limits of their Discipline via study. The Ordo Dracul is all about the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the benefit to NOT giving them Blood Sorcery. Kolduns are great but also there's Biothaumaturgical Experimentation and other Paths that would suit them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-18-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T12:40:15-07:00","id":1418875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any *REAL* Tzimisce fan loves them as sorcerers and mad scientists. No one should want them to be a bunch of flesh crafting losers without magic or their own labs.<br /> <br /> That's not a Tzimisce. That's a poseur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The cusp of Tzimisce philosophy is mostly in the physical and its threshing of it with Vicissitude purely. In some cases they utilize &quot;magic&quot; when need be, but the entirety of their madness and art is from crafting flesh and bone to a multiple of things. That's the ENTIRE BASIS OF THE CLAN. Just look at all the monsters and other entities they make with Vicissitude. Look at their haven and what will you see? An unending wave of flesh and bone furniture as far as the eye can see. Its seldom thought that the Tzimisce AREN'T Flesh-obsessed fiends, so I really don't know where you get &quot;no one should want them be a bunch of flesh crafting &quot;&quot;&quot;losers&quot;&quot;&quot; because that's what the majority (and even people who don't main Tzimisce but are still fond of them) WANT them to be. Where do you get this information from? Also what makes you think they don't have their own labs or personal workshops where they carry out their Vicissitude experiments? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because Serpentis was a joke discipline. They made it actually worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serpentis was much more interesting and tailored specifically to the Setites (and I mean Setites, not the Ministry nonsense) that made them much more interesting. Now their just Gangrel of another name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T12:47:37-07:00","id":1418876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418873#post1418873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Animalism would have no role in Vicissitude. It would just be listing their three Disciplines. I think Blood Sorcery fits the Tzimisce better than Auspex. Because when I think of the ancient lords of the land and traditionalist vampires, I think of Anne Rice Psychic Powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's stupid because I am a HUGE Tzimisce fan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any *REAL* Tzimisce fan loves them as sorcerers and mad scientists. No one should want them to be a bunch of flesh crafting losers without magic or their own labs. That's not a Tzimisce. That's a poseur. Dudes who just go around morphing faces defile the sacred power of the Eldest.<br /> <br /> A real Tzimisce should also seek Koldunism because that's their birthright and sacred power to master their connection with the land.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because Protean is awesome. It needs a power up, though, because shapeshifting should be more versatile than just wolves and bats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, because Serpentis was a joke discipline. They made it actually worthwhile.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Sadly, I feel they ruined the Old Clan Tzimisce or perhaps they made the regular Clan Tzimisce more interesting. The Eldest has Vicissitude and the oldest and most powerful of Tzimisce also have Vicissitude like Yorak. Therefore, there's no point in having Old Clan Tzimisce because Vicissitude is their signature Discipline. Thankfully, since the Old Clan were always 900% more cooler than the regular Clan, merging the two and just forgetting there was any schism over Disciplines in the first place benefits the Tzimisce as a whole.<br /> <br /> Castles, estates, ghouled servants, and weird experiments FTW.<br /> <br /> I will say we've had this argument before but its clear that a lot of people have different ideas on what the Tzimisce SHOULD BE. For me, they are the Clan of not just Dracula but Doctor Frankenstein, Pinhead, mad science, demonic sorcery, Doctor Frank N. Furter, Doctor Giggles, and other creepy B-movie &quot;smart guys are evil.&quot; There's the occasional Tzimisce Surgeon with the Path of Harmony or even Nocturnal Redemption who heals with Vicissitude but they should all be super-duper smart people that are pressing the limits of their Discipline via study. The Ordo Dracul is all about the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the benefit to NOT giving them Blood Sorcery. Kolduns are great but also there's Biothaumaturgical Experimentation and other Paths that would suit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you give them Blood Sorcery, Kolduns will have the same problem Bani Haqim Sorcerers do: They are either good at their clan discipline: Viscittitude and Quietus in these examples OR they have decent Blood Magic, they can't have both due to not being able to have more than one power at a dot, (Also this screws over the Necroscope vibe that is core to what at least a large chunk of Tzim players love)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:10:11-07:00","id":1418878,"title":"","content":"Settites had protean through the lense of faith. Yeah, they had protean, and you should check out the literal meaning of protean, so I don't mind the change all that much, but thematically, it undermines the setites to have their HOLY GOD-GIVEN POWER just be the same shit as the power of the dogs they've historically derided. Settites need a clear division for that to work properly. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, back to vicissitude. <br /> <br /> Things broken about Vicissitude and how to fix them: <br /> <br /> Problem: being able to fuck someone's look up forever by just smearing your hand over their face<br /> Sollution: Give vicissitude a minimum time to be administered properly; a quick smear heals easily, a methodical surgery? that stuff stays forever. Well, if you're at the mercy of a Tzmisce long enough for a methodical surgery, you've been at their mercy long enough to die. Also, I really want to put emphasis on the surgery aspect of the power, so this would help. <br /> <br /> Problem: Raising Appearance (rules are unclear on the limit) <br /> Solution: This is a two step process: Firstly, Put in a fucking limit. Seriously; I don't think all the surgery and photoshop in the world is going to take you beyond 7 or 8 dots of appearance. that's some magical stuff. With V5 that's less significant because you use merits for beauty, and though i'm sure there could be a 6-point beauty standard you can't get at character creation to represent the glorious visage of those blood gods that desperately need an improvement, it wouldn't be a gamechanger. <br /> Secondly: Vicissitude, like real life plastic surgery, is going to have a social stigma to it. Even ignoring religious fears, sectarian fears, general conservatism, and crazy ideas about space aliens, Vicissitude is a nasty discipline to learn (all that trial-and-error leads to a lot of missing animals... or people. All that blood you consume to fuel it... ) <br /> <br /> Problem: It gives you lots of crazy shit like bone spikes that could be OP. <br /> Solution: Procedures. Give that stuff 'rituals' with pros and cons. Document a load of changes, how difficult it is to learn (speculate about how many 'materials' you may need to sacrifice) and give storytellers and surgeons the examples to let them create their own freakish abominations. <br /> <br /> That should do it. Vicissitude stays Vicissitude, and it's awesome for it. <br /> <br /> (also Chimestry stays it's own thing. you leave that alone!) <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Is it strange to feel bad for giving up your good ideas to save an edition you want canceled? What am I doing? </i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:29:14-07:00","id":1418879,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude at its base is a snap Discipline though. Sure old Elders or just any Tzimisce who likes to be methodical and slow in their work (which is the majority line basically), but its an instinctual preternatural ability that can malleate anything at the drop of a hat. Slapping a rude night-jogger in the face who bumped into you whilst using Vicissitude to roll over their skin over their eyes is a display of what its capable of in fast situations. Faux-seducing an unsuspecting woman walking in alone in the secluded part of the park, clasping her hands together under your own clasped ones- lulling her further and further into a false sense of security as you peer into her eyes and chant low soothing murmers, then you release the clasp you have over her hands. When she tries to put her hands to her side, she realizes in collecting horror.. that they just won't budge, being completely fused together and not moving an inch- a thing some Tzimsice would do just for fun. Sneaking into someone's home, then clasping at various parts of their legs to make them much more shorter than usual when they wake up in the morning... all of this is 'just Tzimisce things'. <br /> <br /> I agree with you on the appearance thing.<br /> <br /> The warform abilities are already something a Discipline user of Vicissitude had to work hard to get to. No change would be needed from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:33:03-07:00","id":1418881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418875#post1418875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? The cusp of Tzimisce philosophy is mostly in the physical and its threshing of it with Vicissitude purely. In some cases they utilize &quot;magic&quot; when need be, but the entirety of their madness and art is from crafting flesh and bone to a multiple of things. That's the ENTIRE BASIS OF THE CLAN. Just look at all the monsters and other entities they make with Vicissitude. Look at their haven and what will you see? An unending wave of flesh and bone furniture as far as the eye can see. Its seldom thought that the Tzimisce AREN'T Flesh-obsessed fiends, so I really don't know where you get &quot;no one should want them be a bunch of flesh crafting &quot;&quot;&quot;losers&quot;&quot;&quot; because that's what the majority (and even people who don't main Tzimisce but are still fond of them) WANT them to be. Where do you get this information from? Also what makes you think they don't have their own labs or personal workshops where they carry out their Vicissitude experiments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and merging Vicissitude and Blood Sorcery DRAMATICALLY increases the versatility and variety of experiments they can conduct with Vicissitude. They won't be limited to just flesh crafting when they can do sorcery with it. Besides, all high level Vicissitude functions ALREADY required Blood Sorcery/Thaumaturgy. Its stated the Vozhd, Blood Brothers, Revenants, and other monsters all required Thaumaturgy to create.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Serpentis was much more interesting and tailored specifically to the Setites (and I mean Setites, not the Ministry nonsense) that made them much more interesting. Now their just Gangrel of another name. </div> </div> </div>No, it wasn't. It was underpowered and inflexible with a few cool powers. Don't pretend otherwise. I was the world's biggest Setite fan and everyone knows the Path of Corruption was x1000 better as a Discipline than the Setites' &quot;Signature&quot; discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418876#post1418876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you give them Blood Sorcery, Kolduns will have the same problem Bani Haqim Sorcerers do: They are either good at their clan discipline: Viscittitude and Quietus in these examples OR they have decent Blood Magic, they can't have both due to not being able to have more than one power at a dot, (Also this screws over the Necroscope vibe that is core to what at least a large chunk of Tzim players love)</div> </div> </div> </div>Combo Disciplines means that they can pull off a lot more variety. Basically, in the &quot;Fleshcrafting Mad Scientist&quot; mold, you have Blood Sorcery and Protean but you sacrifice the Protean to provide all the Vicissitude effects while keeping all the Blood Sorcery so you can do all manner of horrifying experiments and not lose any Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> At least that's my take on it.<br /> <br /> But yes, I 100% suggest the Players Guide add an optional rule to allow people to buy as many powers as they want. Vampires should be MORE powerful, not less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Settites had protean through the lense of faith. Yeah, they had protean, and you should check out the literal meaning of protean, so I don't mind the change all that much, but thematically, it undermines the setites to have their HOLY GOD-GIVEN POWER just be the same shit as the power of the dogs they've historically derided. Settites need a clear division for that to work properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for a few flaws in this:<br /> <br /> 1. Their power sucks. Therefore, their HOLY SIGNATURE DISCIPLINE makes them look like losers. Vicissitude, Dementation, Thaumaturgy, and Chimestry are the kind of powers that you can point to and go, &quot;Yeah, I'd be terrified of these people.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. It is the same holy power as every other Clan and Setites believe they're still vampires. It's just other vampires have forgotten that Set is their father.<br /> <br /> 3. Path of Corruption is 100% better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-18-2020, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:35:30-07:00","id":1418882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418881#post1418881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and merging Vicissitude and Blood Sorcery DRAMATICALLY increases the versatility and variety of experiments they can conduct with Vicissitude. They won't be limited to just flesh crafting when they can do sorcery with it. Besides, all high level Vicissitude functions ALREADY required Blood Sorcery/Thaumaturgy. Its stated the Vozhd, Blood Brothers, Revenants, and other monsters all required Thaumaturgy to create.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, it wasn't. It was underpowered and inflexible with a few cool powers. Don't pretend otherwise. I was the world's biggest Setite fan and everyone knows the Path of Corruption was x1000 better as a Discipline than the Setites' &quot;Signature&quot; discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, see the '1 power per dot' point, you are either good at vicissitude or sorcery, not both, under your suggestion. The Same issue Bani Haqim sorcerers have with Quietus/ Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:41:19-07:00","id":1418885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1418620-fanon-thread-how-to-update-the-sabbat-to-5e?p=1418882#post1418882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, see the '1 power per dot' point, you are either good at vicissitude or sorcery, not both, under your suggestion. The Same issue Bani Haqim sorcerers have with Quietus/ Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no, that's not how it works.<br /> <br /> You're good at Blood Sorcery and Vicissitude. Just not good at Protean (which serves as the basis for Vicissitude).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;